# Docker sends the ENTIRE build context to the daemon before running any instruction, and this
# repo's context is ~127 GB: data/ alone is 121 GB of HDF5 + LeRobot datasets, experiments/runs/
# is 3 GB of checkpoints and .git is 2.8 GB. Without these exclusions a `docker build` would
# spend many minutes and tens of GB transferring files the image never uses.
data/
experiments/runs/
results/
.git/
ops/
paper/
notebooks/
**/__pycache__/
*.hdf5
*.tar
# third_party/IsaacLab (87 MB, tag v2.3.0) is deliberately NOT excluded: the image needs it.
